StackEdit 5.15.4
================================================

Upstream: https://github.com/benweet/stackedit (Apache-2.0)
Official release: https://www.npmjs.com/package/stackedit/v/5.15.4
Official image: docker.io/benweet/stackedit:v5.15.4

The unmodified npm source release is stackedit-5.15.4.tgz. The unmodified
final build layer of the official image is docker-build-layer.tar.gz;
its opt/stackedit/dist directory contains the production app, assets, and
source maps with the corresponding bundled module sources. SOURCE.json
records the image manifest and archive digests. The built JavaScript, CSS,
fonts and entry document are served byte for byte; no product code is patched.
server.py and start.sh are local serving and launch scripts. The serving
policy omits source maps, service workers, alternative entry pages, directory
listings and configuration files, and applies Content Security Policy.
Runtime restrictions are documented in the runtime help.

Redistribution notices
----------------------
StackEdit's license is LICENSE; it is also preserved in LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt. Dependencies' original
notices are under LICENSES/third-party; they are taken from the exact npm
install in the official image, or the corresponding package/source release.
For delegate, good-listener and select, the distributed package README
provides the MIT grant link and Zeno Rocha attribution; the MIT terms are
included with that attribution. markdown-it-imsize declares MIT and author
tatsy; its full MIT terms and attribution are included. Babel and regenerator
notices come from their upstream source repositories. The original module
source is also in the image build layer's source maps.
Lato fonts use OFL-1.1; Roboto Mono uses Apache-2.0. normalize-scss is used
under its MIT option, and linkify-it under its MIT option where dual-licensed.
The entities package's BSD-like notice is the two-clause BSD license.

